  {
   "i": 57,
   "shape_h": "ol",
   "shape_m": "ol",
   "html_text": "Is variation targeted, in the sense that the production of variants is biased towards producing some possible variants (i.e., “non-random”)? Is variation subject to developmental filtering and modification before transmission, as found for example in behavioral inheritance? Is variation constructed through direct planning by the organisms? Can variations change the selective environment, for example by changing the environmental niche the organism occupies?",
